  "question": {
    "text": "A photoelectric material having work-function <math><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is illuminated with a light of wavelength <math><mi>λ</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>. The fastest photoelectron has a de Broglie wavelength <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></math>. A change in wavelength of the incident light by <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>λ</mi></math> results in a change <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></math> in <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></math>. The ratio <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is proportional to"
  },
